<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <RootNamespace>Delibera.Server</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Delibera.Server</AssemblyName>
    <UserSecretsId>delibera-server-secrets</UserSecretsId>
    <DockerDefaultTargetOS>Linux</DockerDefaultTargetOS>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet package metadata.
       Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web does not inherit the library defaults, so every field Core gets for
       free has to be stated here: otherwise the package ships with no description, no licence
       expression and no icon, and nuget.org rejects it. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Delibera.Server</PackageId>
    <!-- Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web sets IsPackable=false because the Web SDK's default output is an
         app, not a library. This project ships as a reusable library, so it must opt back in. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <Version>10.5.3</Version>
    <Title>Delibera Server</Title>
    <Description>ASP.NET Core host for the Delibera multi-model AI council framework: debate, scenario, corpus, SSE streaming and MCP endpoints mountable inside an existing application through AddDeliberaServer/UseDeliberaServer. All routes live under /api/v1 so they cannot collide with your own endpoints. Depends on Delibera.Core.</Description>
    <Authors>Victor Buzin</Authors>
    <PackageTags>llm;ai;debate;council;deliberation;aspnetcore;minimal-api;server;api;sse;server-sent-events;mcp;model-context-protocol;rag;opentelemetry;serilog;multi-model</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/techbuzzz/Delibera</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/techbuzzz/Delibera</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v10.5.3 — BuiltIn constants, opt-in CORS, project website, Web UI fixes and performance. No breaking changes.

New — opt-in CORS for static browser clients. `Delibera:Server:Cors:AllowedOrigins` registers a named CORS policy listing the browser origins permitted to call the API cross-origin, and `UseCors` is wired only when that list is non-empty. Off by default: the Web UI reaches the API through its own same-origin BFF route and never needs CORS. Origins are matched exactly; there is no wildcard switch. `AllowCredentials` together with `*` is rejected at startup with a message naming the config key.

New — BuiltIn constants extracted across Delibera.Core. A single source of truth for HTTP headers, SSE event names, config sections, role names and other magic strings that previously drifted between projects. SSE event names remain a contract with the Web UI.

Fixed — three per-request costs on the server. ValidationFilter cached validator type resolution per argument type. RedisDebateOrchestrator now reuses the injected ConnectionMultiplexer instead of opening its own. The SSE writer assembles each frame once in the response pipe and flushes once, with event names as u8 literals.

Fixed — the proxy kept upstream SSE connections open after the browser left. The proxy now aborts its own fetch when the response closes before it was fully written.

Fixed — Web UI behaviours: cancel now distinguishes "cancelled" from "already finished"; changing a filter reloads from page 1; npm test now builds first via pretest so it passes on a clean checkout; the live view announces rounds to screen readers via a polite live region; every route titles itself; hover states and visible focus rings added.

Fixed — the Web UI typecheck was passing while silently checking less. Nuxt upgraded to 4.6.1, vue-router to ^5.4.0 matching it, vue-tsc to 3.3, vitest to 5, @nuxt/test-utils to 4. The check is clean for the first time.

Changed — Node is pinned to an exact patch (22.23.3), because nuxt@4.6.1 declares engines.node: ^22.22.3 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0.

New — GitHub Pages deploys the project website (Next.js static export in site/), not the Web UI. The site reads the version from Delibera.Core.csproj at build time, renders docs at any depth, and serves release notes, measurements, and debate templates extracted from source.

CI — Docker Hub publish is now behind an environment (dockerhub-prod), like NuGet (nuget-prod). Release workflow creates the GitHub Release page from docs/WhatsNew-*.md. Merge commits are used instead of squash so ancestry checks remain meaningful.

Tests: Core + Server + gRPC tests passing, plus Web UI tests (API contract + SSE streaming). Clean under -warnaserror.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- icon.png and README.md must physically exist next to the csproj: a PackageIcon or
       PackageReadmeFile pointing at ..\..\ does not resolve during pack. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Core -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Delibera.Core\Delibera.Core.csproj" />
    <!-- Redis: opt-in distributed debate state, gated by Delibera:Redis:Enabled.
         This becomes a package dependency of Delibera.Server on nuget.org — accepted
         deliberately. Delibera.Redis ships in the same GA matrix (publish-nuget.yml),
         both are versioned together, and the alternative (PrivateAssets="all") would
         remove AddRedisDebateOrchestrator from the published package, which is the one
         thing this reference exists to expose. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Delibera.Redis\Delibera.Redis.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- ASP.NET / Minimal API -->
    <!-- Microsoft.OpenApi 3.x makes IOpenApiMediaType.Example read-only, which breaks
         the AspNetCore.OpenApi source generator (it emits Example = ... in the
         generated OpenApiXmlCommentSupport code). Pin to 2.7.x until the source
         generator is updated for v3.
         Evidence: with Microsoft.OpenApi 3.10.2 and Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi
         10.0.12 the generator still emits `Example = ...` assignments against the
         read-only IOpenApiMediaType.Example, and the build fails with CS0200
         (CS0200: property or indexer 'Example' cannot be assigned to, it is read only)
         inside generated OpenApiXmlCommentSupport code. Re-tested and reverted
         3.10.2 -> 2.7.5 for the 10.4.0 release gate; do not retry 3.x until the
         generator ships v3-aware emission.
         The floor matters: Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0.12 declares
         Microsoft.OpenApi [2.12.0, 3.0.0), so an explicit 2.7.5 pin does not restore —
         it is NU1605 (detected package downgrade 2.12.0 -> 2.7.5), which is an error here.
         2.12.2 is the last published 2.x, so it is both the floor-satisfying pin and the
         highest version that still has the settable IOpenApiMediaType.Example. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.OpenApi" Version="2.12.2" />

    <!-- MCP Server (HTTP transport) -->
    <PackageReference Include="ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore" Version="2.2.0" />

    <!-- Validation -->
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="12.1.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions" Version="12.1.1" />

    <!-- Observability -->
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting" Version="1.19.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNetCore" Version="1.19.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http" Version="1.19.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.Console" Version="1.19.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol" Version="1.19.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Runtime" Version="1.19.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog.AspNetCore" Version="10.0.0" />
    <!-- NU1510: Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Extensions and                                        -->
    <!--         Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics.HealthChecks are implicit in                  -->
    <!--         Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web — removed explicit references.                           -->
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
